    // D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col
    // lays them out (f16 A and B, f16 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.
    // ucas mma m16n8k8 f16 under mali_g715: output-stationary; A: 6 loads from shared memory (register-major); B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); k order by lane;
    // cost 563.14 (each word fetched from its lane: 0).
    // Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;
    // |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), then D's f16 rounding, u = 2^-24.
    #ifndef MMA_WARPS
    #define MMA_WARPS 1  // the workgroup's warps of 32
